        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$AB=BC=AC=2$. Equilateral (all sides equal).",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}AB&=\\sqrt{(1-(-1))^2+(0-0)^2}\\\\AB&=2\\\\BC&=\\sqrt{(0-1)^2+(\\sqrt{3}-0)^2}\\\\BC&=2\\\\AC&=\\sqrt{(0-(-1))^2+(\\sqrt{3}-0)^2}\\\\AC&=2\\end{align*}$$\nAll three sides are equal, so the triangle is equilateral.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$P(-1,1),\\ Q(0,-1),\\ R(3,3)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$PQ=\\sqrt{5}$, $QR=5$, $PR=2\\sqrt{5}$. Right-angled at $P$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}PQ&=\\sqrt{(0-(-1))^2+(-1-1)^2}\\\\PQ&=\\sqrt{5}\\\\QR&=\\sqrt{(3-0)^2+(3-(-1))^2}\\\\QR&=5\\\\PR&=\\sqrt{(3-(-1))^2+(3-1)^2}\\\\PR&=\\sqrt{20}=2\\sqrt{5}\\\\PQ^2+PR^2&=5+20\\\\PQ^2+PR^2&=25=QR^2\\end{align*}$$\nBy Pythagoras’ theorem, the triangle is right-angled at $P$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 57
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$D(1,1),\\ E(2,-2),\\ F(-3,0)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$DE=\\sqrt{10}$, $EF=\\sqrt{29}$, $DF=\\sqrt{17}$. None of the above: scalene and not right-angled.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}DE&=\\sqrt{(2-1)^2+(-2-1)^2}\\\\DE&=\\sqrt{10}\\\\EF&=\\sqrt{(-3-2)^2+(0-(-2))^2}\\\\EF&=\\sqrt{29}\\\\DF&=\\sqrt{(-3-1)^2+(0-1)^2}\\\\DF&=\\sqrt{17}\\\\DE^2+DF^2&=10+17\\\\DE^2+DF^2&=27\\ne29=EF^2\\end{align*}$$\nAll side lengths differ, so the triangle is scalene. The two shorter sides do not satisfy Pythagoras’ theorem with the longest side, so it is not right-angled. Hence it is none of the listed types.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q9-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$X(-3,-1),\\ Y(0,0),\\ Z(-2,2)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$XY=XZ=\\sqrt{10}$, $YZ=\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2}$. Isosceles.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}XY&=\\sqrt{(0-(-3))^2+(0-(-1))^2}\\\\XY&=\\sqrt{10}\\\\YZ&=\\sqrt{(-2-0)^2+(2-0)^2}\\\\YZ&=\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2}\\\\XZ&=\\sqrt{(-2-(-3))^2+(2-(-1))^2}\\\\XZ&=\\sqrt{10}\\end{align*}$$\nSince $XY=XZ$, the triangle is isosceles.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      }
    ]
  },
